 "discovery_answer": "I registered the egress answer. This is what `nookku register` printed:\n\n```\nnookku: the egress answer is registered. The next start uses these parts:\n- model API anthropic: ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL -> the URL in ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL or the default (proxy)\n- MCP server catalog: http CATALOG_MCP_URL -> http://127.0.0.1:9310/mcp (proxy)\n- MCP server notes: stdio NOTES_MCP_COMMAND -> python3 notes_mcp.py (proxy)\n- database shop: postgres, DATABASE_URL (proxy)\n- database returns: sqlite, returns.db (driver trace)\n```\n\nWhere each part comes from in `app.py`:\n- **anthropic:** the Claude Agent SDK session, which uses the `haiku` model. The app doesn't set a base URL.\n- **catalog:** the HTTP MCP server. Its URL comes from `CATALOG_MCP_URL` (`app.py:36`).\n- **notes:** the stdio MCP server. The app reads its command line from `NOTES_MCP_COMMAND` and splits it into words (`app.py:37`, `app.py:120`). The `notes.json` file it writes is part of that server, so it isn't listed separately.\n- **shop:** the Postgres database that `lookup_order` reads with psycopg. Its `postgres://` URL comes from `DATABASE_URL`, so the proxy records the calls.\n- **returns:** the SQLite file `returns.db` that `start_return` writes.\n\nThere are no HTTP backends or other parts.\n\n**Driver trace:** I didn't change the agent's code. It already turns on the psycopg and sqlite3 instrumentations and sends their spans over OTLP/HTTP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set (`app.py:45-69`). Nookku sets that variable during the test, and the spans include the statement text. The `returns` SQLite calls are recorded only through this trace. It has no result rows and may hide parameter values, so the record shows the SQL but not always the values inserted.\n\nPlease check the parts. If they're right, type `nookku start` within the next 30 minutes. If a part is wrong, tell me what to change and I'll register the answer again.",
